    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d880">

                <pb facs="1119" n="1017" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg1017"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">452.11/326</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 908</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-02">October 2,
                        1935</date>.<lb/>[Received October 15.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my despatch No. 833 of
                    July 27,<anchor n="27" xml:id="d880-f1"/> I have the honor to report that I had
                    an interview with the Minister for Foreign Affairs this morning regarding the
                    American claims in the Spanish Zone in Morocco and urged upon him the adoption
                    of the formula given in my cable No. 6 of January 14, 3 p.m. I pointed out that
                    we have now waited nine months for a reply which it was originally expected
                    could be given within ten days and that since the High Commissioner of the
                    Spanish Zone Sr. Rico Avello, is now in Madrid the present moment is a
                    propitious one in which to come to some definite conclusion.</p>
                <p>Sr. Lerroux said that the above referred to formula had been brought to his
                    attention when he was Prime Minister and that he would request the
                    Under-Secretary of the Ministry for Foreign Affairs immediately to get in touch
                    with Sr. Rico Avello. He added that he would be “diligent” in seeking an
                    arrangement of this question and that he desired American recognition of the
                    Spanish Zone.</p>
                <p>I left with Sr. Lerroux an <hi rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi> based on the
                    Department’s cable No. 15 of February 21, 6 p.m., bringing to his personal
                    attention the facts of the situation and the long delay thus far
                    experienced.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Claude G. Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
